This software is not yet released under an open-source licence. No permission is
granted to copy, modify, distribute or use it except by the copyright holder and
those he has authorised directly.

Why this file says that rather than naming a licence: the package is the portable
half of a deliberate three-way split (see "IP separation" in README.md). The physics
structure, the detector bank and the corpus schema are generalizable expertise and
are worth licensing on purpose rather than by default. Choosing the licence is a
decision for the copyright holder, and until it is made the conservative statement
above is the accurate one.

The plant-specific half -- config.json, fitted constants, station and register maps --
and the operational half -- twin_log.csv, signatures.jsonl, labels.jsonl -- belong to
the plant owner and are not covered by this repository at all. Neither is
committed here, and .gitignore is set up to keep it that way.
